// Test: `hasServerField` on a resolver root fragment's split operation.
//
// The flag answers one question — can this resolver produce a value before the
// response is normalized? It cannot if its root fragment reads any server field,
// because that data does not exist yet. The exec-time executor uses it to decide
// whether to evaluate the resolver while building the execution tree, or to
// leave it to the post-normalization drain.
//
